{"schemaVersion":2,"bookId":"mackay-information-theory-2003","title":"第 16 章　消息传递","sourcePdfPages":[253,259],"toc":[{"number":"16","title":"消息传递","block":"p253-b001"},{"number":"16.1","title":"计数","block":"p253-b004"},{"number":"16.2","title":"路径计数","block":"p256-b001"},{"number":"16.3","title":"寻找最低成本路径","block":"p257-b005"},{"number":"16.4","title":"总结与相关想法","block":"p258-b007"},{"number":"16.5","title":"补充习题","block":"p258-b011"},{"number":"16.6","title":"解答","block":"p259-b001"}],"blocks":[{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"heading","level":1,"text":"第 16 章　消息传递","segments":["第 16 章　消息传递"],"id":"p253-b001"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"intro","text":"编者导读（非原书正文）　本章从排队士兵的计数规则出发，展示简单节点怎样通过局部消息完成全局计算；随后讨论网格路径的计数、随机路径采样和最低成本路径。","segments":[{"strong":true,"text":"编者导读（非原书正文）"},"　本章从排队士兵的计数规则出发，展示简单节点怎样通过局部消息完成全局计算；随后讨论网格路径的计数、随机路径采样和最低成本路径。"],"id":"p253-b002"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"paragraph","text":"本书的一个主题，是用简单的分布式硬件完成复杂计算。事实证明，不少有趣的问题可以通过消息传递算法解决：简单处理器在局部交换简短消息，经过一段时间，各处理器的运算共同求出一个全局问题的答案。","segments":["本书的一个主题，是用简单的分布式硬件完成复杂计算。事实证明，不少有趣的问题可以通过",{"em":true,"text":"消息传递"},"算法解决：简单处理器在局部交换简短消息，经过一段时间，各处理器的运算共同求出一个全局问题的答案。"],"id":"p253-b003"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"16.1　计数","segments":["16.1　计数"],"id":"p253-b004"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"paragraph","text":"举例来说，设想一队士兵正在雾中行进。指挥官想完成一项复杂的计算：数出队伍里有多少名士兵。这个问题有两种解法。","segments":["举例来说，设想一队士兵正在雾中行进。指挥官想完成一项复杂的计算：数出队伍里有多少名士兵。这个问题有两种解法。"],"id":"p253-b005"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一种解法需要昂贵的“硬件”：指挥官和士兵洪亮的嗓门。指挥官可以喊：“所有士兵，一分钟内向我报到！”然后仔细听士兵一个个回答：“Molesworth 报到，长官！”“Fotherington–Thomas 报到，长官！”等等。这种解法依赖好几种昂贵的“硬件”：每名士兵与指挥官之间都必须有可靠的双向通信渠道；指挥官必须能听清所有来报到的消息——即使有几百名士兵——还必须会数数；若士兵与指挥官之间可能相隔很远，士兵还得吃饱饭，才喊得回去。","segments":["第一种解法需要昂贵的“硬件”：指挥官和士兵洪亮的嗓门。指挥官可以喊：“所有士兵，一分钟内向我报到！”然后仔细听士兵一个个回答：“Molesworth 报到，长官！”“Fotherington–Thomas 报到，长官！”等等。这种解法依赖好几种昂贵的“硬件”：每名士兵与指挥官之间都必须有可靠的双向通信渠道；指挥官必须能听清所有来报到的消息——即使有几百名士兵——还必须会数数；若士兵与指挥官之间可能相隔很远，士兵还得吃饱饭，才喊得回去。"],"id":"p253-b006"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二种求士兵总数的解法，不需要全局通信设备、高智商或好伙食；只要求每名士兵能与队伍中相邻的两名士兵传递单个整数，并能给一个数加 $1$。每名士兵按下列规则行事：","segments":["第二种求士兵总数的解法，不需要全局通信设备、高智商或好伙食；只要求每名士兵能与队伍中相邻的两名士兵传递单个整数，并能给一个数加 ",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"。每名士兵按下列规则行事："],"id":"p253-b007"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"paragraph","text":"算法 16.1　消息传递规则集 A","segments":[{"strong":true,"text":"算法 16.1　消息传递规则集 A"}],"id":"p253-b008"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"text":"如果你是队伍最前面的士兵，就对身后的士兵报数“$1$”。","segments":["如果你是队伍最前面的士兵，就对身后的士兵报数“",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"”。"]},{"text":"如果你是队伍最后面的士兵，就对前面的士兵报数“$1$”。","segments":["如果你是队伍最后面的士兵，就对前面的士兵报数“",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"”。"]},{"text":"如果前方或后方的士兵向你报了一个数，就给这个数加 $1$，再把新数报给另一侧的士兵。","segments":["如果前方或后方的士兵向你报了一个数，就给这个数加 ",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"，再把新数报给另一侧的士兵。"]}],"id":"p253-b009"},{"pdfPage":253,"page":1,"kind":"paragraph","text":"如果聪明的指挥官不仅会给一个数加 $1$，还会把两个数相加，那么他只须把接续下页的三项相加，就能得到士兵总数：","segments":["如果聪明的指挥官不仅会给一个数加 ",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"，还会把两个数相加，那么他只须把接续下页的三项相加，就能得到士兵总数："],"id":"p253-b010"},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"table","rows":[[{"text":"","segments":[],"header":false},{"text":"前面的士兵告诉指挥官的数","segments":["前面的士兵告诉指挥官的数"],"header":false},{"text":"（它等于前方士兵的总数）","segments":["（它等于前方士兵的总数）"],"header":false}],[{"text":"＋","segments":["＋"],"header":false},{"text":"后面的士兵告诉指挥官的数","segments":["后面的士兵告诉指挥官的数"],"header":false},{"text":"（它等于后方士兵的总数）","segments":["（它等于后方士兵的总数）"],"header":false}],[{"text":"＋","segments":["＋"],"header":false},{"text":"一","segments":["一"],"header":false},{"text":"（把指挥官本人也算进去）","segments":["（把指挥官本人也算进去）"],"header":false}]],"id":"p254-b001"},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"paragraph","text":"这种解法只需局部通信设备和简单的计算（存储整数并把整数相加）。","segments":["这种解法只需局部通信设备和简单的计算（存储整数并把整数相加）。"],"id":"p254-b002"},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-2.png","width":1125,"height":300,"alt":"图 16.2：队列中五名士兵互相传递计数消息","caption":"图 16.2　一队士兵按消息传递规则集 A 数出自身人数。图内的 “Commander” 是指挥官；上方箭头从左向右依次传 $1,2,3,4$，下方箭头从右向左依次传 $1,2,3,4$。指挥官把前方士兵报来的 $3$、后方士兵报来的 $1$，以及自己的 $1$ 相加，得出共有 $5$ 名士兵。","captionSegments":["图 16.2　一队士兵按消息传递规则集 A 数出自身人数。图内的 “Commander” 是指挥官；上方箭头从左向右依次传 ",{"tex":"1,2,3,4","text":"1,2,3,4","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>"},"，下方箭头从右向左依次传 ",{"tex":"1,2,3,4","text":"1,2,3,4","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>"},"。指挥官把前方士兵报来的 ",{"tex":"3","text":"3","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>"},"、后方士兵报来的 ",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"，以及自己的 ",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"}," 相加，得出共有 ",{"tex":"5","text":"5","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>"}," 名士兵。"],"id":"p254-b003","wide":true},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"heading","level":3,"text":"分离性","segments":[{"em":true,"text":"分离性"}],"id":"p254-b004"},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"paragraph","text":"这个巧妙办法利用了士兵总数的一个重要性质：它可以写成某一点前方的士兵数与该点后方的士兵数之和。这两个量可以分别计算，因为指挥官把两组士兵隔开了。","segments":["这个巧妙办法利用了士兵总数的一个重要性质：它可以写成某一点",{"em":true,"text":"前方"},"的士兵数与该点",{"em":true,"text":"后方"},"的士兵数之和。这两个量可以",{"em":true,"text":"分别"},"计算，因为指挥官把两组士兵隔开了。"],"id":"p254-b005"},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"paragraph","text":"如果士兵不是排成一列，而是成群行进，就不容易像这样把他们分成两组。图 16.3 中的游击队员不能使用上述消息传递规则集 A 来计数：虽然他们各有邻居（图中以线段表示），但不清楚谁在“前面”、谁在“后面”；而且，他们的连接图中有环，所以环上的游击队员（例如 Jim）无法把队伍分成“前面的人”和“后面的人”两组。","segments":["如果士兵不是排成一列，而是成群行进，就不容易像这样把他们分成两组。图 16.3 中的游击队员不能使用上述消息传递规则集 A 来计数：虽然他们各有邻居（图中以线段表示），但不清楚谁在“前面”、谁在“后面”；而且，他们的连接",{"em":true,"text":"图"},"中有环，所以环上的游击队员（例如 Jim）无法把队伍",{"em":true,"text":"分成"},"“前面的人”和“后面的人”两组。"],"id":"p254-b006"},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-3.png","width":1175,"height":825,"alt":"图 16.3：含有环的游击队员连接图","caption":"图 16.3　一群游击队员。图内 “Commander” 是指挥官，“Jim” 是 Jim；线段表示队员之间的连接，其中有环。","captionSegments":["图 16.3　一群游击队员。图内 “Commander” 是指挥官，“Jim” 是 Jim；线段表示队员之间的连接，其中有环。"],"id":"p254-b007","wide":true},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"paragraph","text":"只要游击队员之间的连接图没有环，就可以用修改后的消息传递算法数出这群人的总数。","segments":[{"em":true,"text":"只要游击队员之间的连接图没有环"},"，就可以用修改后的消息传递算法数出这群人的总数。"],"id":"p254-b008"},{"pdfPage":254,"page":2,"kind":"paragraph","text":"规则集 B 是一种消息传递算法，用于统计连接关系构成无环图（cycle-free graph，又称树）的游击队员人数，如图 16.4 所示。任何一名游击队员都能根据自己收到的消息，推算树中的总人数。","segments":["规则集 B 是一种消息传递算法，用于统计连接关系构成无环图（cycle-free graph，又称树）的游击队员人数，如图 16.4 所示。任何一名游击队员都能根据自己收到的消息，推算树中的总人数。"],"id":"p254-b009"},{"pdfPage":255,"page":3,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-4.png","width":1175,"height":825,"alt":"图 16.4：连接关系构成树的游击队员","caption":"图 16.4　一群连接关系构成树的游击队员。图内 “Commander” 是指挥官，“Jim” 是 Jim；各线段连接队员，图中没有环。","captionSegments":["图 16.4　一群连接关系构成树的游击队员。图内 “Commander” 是指挥官，“Jim” 是 Jim；各线段连接队员，图中没有环。"],"id":"p255-b001","wide":true},{"pdfPage":255,"page":3,"kind":"paragraph","text":"算法 16.5　消息传递规则集 B","segments":[{"strong":true,"text":"算法 16.5　消息传递规则集 B"}],"id":"p255-b002"},{"pdfPage":255,"page":3,"kind":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"text":"数一数自己有多少个邻居，记为 $N$。","segments":["数一数自己有多少个邻居，记为 ",{"tex":"N","text":"N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>"},"。"]},{"text":"记录已经从邻居收到的消息数 $m$，以及各条消息的值 $v_1,v_2,\\ldots,v_N$。令 $V$ 为目前收到的消息值之和。","segments":["记录已经从邻居收到的消息数 ",{"tex":"m","text":"m","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></math>"},"，以及各条消息的值 ",{"tex":"v_1,v_2,\\ldots,v_N","text":"v_1,v_2,\\ldots,v_N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></math>"},"。令 ",{"tex":"V","text":"V","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow></math>"}," 为目前收到的消息值之和。"]},{"text":"如果已收到的消息数 $m=N-1$，找出还没有向你发消息的邻居，把数 $V+1$ 告诉他。","segments":["如果已收到的消息数 ",{"tex":"m=N-1","text":"m=N-1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"，找出还没有向你发消息的邻居，把数 ",{"tex":"V+1","text":"V+1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"}," 告诉他。"]},{"text":"如果已收到的消息数 $m=N$，那么：","segments":["如果已收到的消息数 ",{"tex":"m=N","text":"m=N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>"},"，那么："]}],"id":"p255-b003"},{"pdfPage":255,"page":3,"kind":"paragraph","text":"(a) 数 $V+1$ 就是所求的总人数。","segments":["(a) 数 ",{"tex":"V+1","text":"V+1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"}," 就是所求的总人数。"],"id":"p255-b004"},{"pdfPage":255,"page":3,"kind":"paragraph","text":"(b) 对每个邻居 $n$ {\n　向邻居 $n$ 报数 $V+1-v_n$。\n}","segments":["(b) 对每个邻居 ",{"tex":"n","text":"n","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>"}," {","\n　向邻居 ",{"tex":"n","text":"n","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>"}," 报数 ",{"tex":"V+1-v_n","text":"V+1-v_n","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></math>"},"。","\n}"],"id":"p255-b005"},{"pdfPage":255,"page":3,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-6.png","width":725,"height":800,"alt":"图 16.6：三角形四十一乘四十一网格中的一条路径","caption":"图 16.6　一个三角形的 $41\\times41$ 网格。从 $A$ 到 $B$ 有多少条路径？图中用粗线示出其中一条。","captionSegments":["图 16.6　一个三角形的 ",{"tex":"41\\times41","text":"41\\times41","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow></math>"}," 网格。从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 有多少条路径？图中用粗线示出其中一条。"],"id":"p255-b006","wide":true},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"16.2　路径计数","segments":["16.2　路径计数"],"id":"p256-b001"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"比数士兵更深入的任务，是数出穿过一个网格的路径总数，以及有多少条路径经过网格中的任意给定点。","segments":["比数士兵更深入的任务，是数出穿过一个网格的路径总数，以及有多少条路径经过网格中的任意给定点。"],"id":"p256-b002"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"图 16.6 给出一个矩形网格，以及连接 $A$、$B$ 两点的一条路径。合法路径从 $A$ 出发，只向右或向下移动，直到 $B$。我们要问：","segments":["图 16.6 给出一个矩形网格，以及连接 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"},"、",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 两点的一条路径。合法路径从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 出发，只向右或向下移动，直到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"},"。我们要问："],"id":"p256-b003"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"text":"从 $A$ 到 $B$ 这样的路径共有多少条？","segments":["从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 这样的路径共有多少条？"]},{"text":"如果随机选取一条从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的路径，它经过网格中某个特定节点的概率是多少？［这里的“随机”，是指所有路径被选中的概率完全相同。］","segments":["如果随机选取一条从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径，它经过网格中某个特定节点的概率是多少？［这里的“随机”，是指所有",{"em":true,"text":"路径"},"被选中的概率完全相同。］"]},{"text":"怎样随机选取一条从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的路径？","segments":["怎样随机选取一条从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径？"]}],"id":"p256-b004"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"数出从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的所有路径，乍看并不容易。路径数应该相当大：即使只允许走一条宽度仅为三个节点的对角带，也仍会有约 $2^{N/2}$ 条可走路径。","segments":["数出从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的所有路径，乍看并不容易。路径数应该相当大：即使只允许走一条宽度仅为三个节点的对角带，也仍会有约 ",{"tex":"2^{N/2}","text":"2^{N/2}","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>"}," 条可走路径。"],"id":"p256-b005"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"计算上的关键突破在于：要找到路径条数，无须显式列举所有路径。取网格中的一点 $P$，考虑从 $A$ 到 $P$ 有多少条路径。每条从 $A$ 到 $P$ 的路径，都必须从 $P$ 的某个上游邻居进入 $P$；这里的“上游”是指上方或左方。因此，把从 $A$ 到这些邻居的路径数相加，就得到从 $A$ 到 $P$ 的路径数。","segments":["计算上的关键突破在于：要找到路径",{"em":true,"text":"条数"},"，无须显式列举所有路径。取网格中的一点 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"},"，考虑从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 有多少条路径。每条从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径，都必须从 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的某个上游邻居进入 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"},"；这里的“上游”是指上方或左方。因此，把从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到这些邻居的路径数相加，就得到从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径数。"],"id":"p256-b006"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-7.png","width":550,"height":450,"alt":"图 16.7：从 A 到 P 的路径由上游邻居进入 P","caption":"图 16.7　每条从 $A$ 到 $P$ 的路径，都从 $P$ 的一个上游邻居进入 $P$，即 $M$ 或 $N$。所以，从 $A$ 到 $P$ 的路径数，等于从 $A$ 到 $M$ 的路径数与从 $A$ 到 $N$ 的路径数之和。图中的箭头给出向右、向下的移动方向。","captionSegments":["图 16.7　每条从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径，都从 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的一个上游邻居进入 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"},"，即 ",{"tex":"M","text":"M","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></math>"}," 或 ",{"tex":"N","text":"N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>"},"。所以，从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径数，等于从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"M","text":"M","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径数与从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"N","text":"N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径数之和。图中的箭头给出向右、向下的移动方向。"],"id":"p256-b007"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"图 16.8 在一个简单网格上演示这一消息传递算法。该网格有十个顶点，由十二条有向边连接。我们从 $A$ 发出数值为“$1$”的消息。当某个节点收齐所有上游邻居的消息后，就把这些值的和传给下游邻居。到达 $B$ 时，得到数 $5$：我们没有逐一枚举路径，却已数出从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的路径条数。图 16.9 画出这五条不同路径，可用来核对结果。","segments":["图 16.8 在一个简单网格上演示这一消息传递算法。该网格有十个顶点，由十二条有向边连接。我们从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 发出数值为“",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"”的消息。当某个节点收齐所有上游邻居的消息后，就把这些值的",{"em":true,"text":"和"},"传给下游邻居。到达 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 时，得到数 ",{"tex":"5","text":"5","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>"},"：我们没有逐一枚举路径，却已数出从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径条数。图 16.9 画出这五条不同路径，可用来核对结果。"],"id":"p256-b008"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-8.png","width":625,"height":450,"alt":"图 16.8：路径计数的前向消息","caption":"图 16.8　前向传递的消息。图中各数字是从 $A$ 到相应节点的路径数；到 $B$ 的数值为 $5$。","captionSegments":["图 16.8　前向传递的消息。图中各数字是从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到相应节点的路径数；到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的数值为 ",{"tex":"5","text":"5","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>"},"。"],"id":"p256-b009","wide":true},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-9.png","width":625,"height":465,"alt":"图 16.9：从 A 到 B 的五条路径","caption":"图 16.9　从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的五条路径。","captionSegments":["图 16.9　从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的五条路径。"],"id":"p256-b010","wide":true},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"数出全部路径后，我们可以继续处理更难的问题：求随机路径经过某个给定顶点的概率，以及实际生成一条随机路径。","segments":["数出全部路径后，我们可以继续处理更难的问题：求随机路径经过某个给定顶点的概率，以及实际生成一条随机路径。"],"id":"p256-b011"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"heading","level":3,"text":"经过节点的概率","segments":[{"em":true,"text":"经过节点的概率"}],"id":"p256-b012"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"除了前向传递，再做一次反向传递，就能算出经过每个节点的路径条数；再除以路径总数，便得到随机选取的路径经过该节点的概率。图 16.10 将反向传递的消息标在各方格右下角，原先前向传递的消息标在左上角。把某个顶点处的这两个数相乘，就得到经过该顶点的路径总数。例如，经过中央顶点的路径有四条。","segments":["除了前向传递，再做一次反向传递，就能算出经过每个节点的路径条数；再除以路径总数，便得到随机选取的路径经过该节点的概率。图 16.10 将反向传递的消息标在各方格右下角，原先前向传递的消息标在左上角。把某个顶点处的这两个数相乘，就得到经过该顶点的路径总数。例如，经过中央顶点的路径有四条。"],"id":"p256-b013"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-10.png","width":625,"height":500,"alt":"图 16.10：前向与反向传递的路径计数消息","caption":"图 16.10　前向和反向传递的消息。每个节点方格左上角是从 $A$ 到该节点的路径数，右下角是从该节点到 $B$ 的路径数；两数的乘积给出经过该节点的路径数。","captionSegments":["图 16.10　前向和反向传递的消息。每个节点方格左上角是从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到该节点的路径数，右下角是从该节点到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径数；两数的乘积给出经过该节点的路径数。"],"id":"p256-b014","wide":true},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"paragraph","text":"图 16.11 展示了对 $41\\times41$ 三角形网格进行这一计算的结果。图中每个黑色斑点的面积，与路径经过相应节点的概率成正比。","segments":["图 16.11 展示了对 ",{"tex":"41\\times41","text":"41\\times41","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow></math>"}," 三角形网格进行这一计算的结果。图中每个黑色斑点的面积，与路径经过相应节点的概率成正比。"],"id":"p256-b015"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"kind":"heading","level":3,"text":"随机路径采样","segments":[{"em":true,"text":"随机路径采样"}],"id":"p256-b016"},{"pdfPage":256,"page":4,"recommendedIcon":"assets/shared/exercise-rat.png","kind":"exercise","label":"习题 16.1","text":"［难度 1；解答见原书印刷页 247］如果在每个可以选择两个方向的交叉点，都掷一枚公平硬币来生成从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的“随机”路径，那么得到的路径是从全部路径中均匀随机抽取的吗？［提示：试着在图 16.8 的网格上这样做。］","segments":["［难度 1；解答见原书印刷页 247］如果在每个可以选择两个方向的交叉点，都掷一枚公平硬币来生成从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的“随机”路径，那么得到的路径是从全部路径中均匀随机抽取的吗？［提示：试着在图 16.8 的网格上这样做。］"],"id":"p256-b017"},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"kind":"paragraph","text":"这里有一个巧妙的思路；我希望你能享受到自己想出答案的乐趣。","segments":["这里有一个巧妙的思路；我希望你能享受到自己想出答案的乐趣。"],"id":"p257-b001"},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"recommendedIcon":"assets/shared/exercise-rat.png","kind":"exercise","label":"习题 16.2","text":"［难度 2；解答见原书印刷页 247］已经在网格上对 $A$ 与 $B$ 之间的路径运行前向和反向算法，怎样从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的全部路径中均匀地随机抽取一条？（见图 16.11。）","segments":["［难度 2；解答见原书印刷页 247］已经在网格上对 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 与 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 之间的路径运行前向和反向算法，怎样从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的全部路径中",{"em":true,"text":"均匀地"},"随机抽取一条？（见图 16.11。）"],"id":"p257-b002"},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-11.png","width":1350,"height":675,"alt":"图 16.11：各节点的经过概率与随机选取的一条路径","caption":"图 16.11　(a) 路径经过各节点的概率；(b) 随机选取的一条路径。左图黑色斑点的面积表示相应概率，右图的黑色折线表示从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的样本路径。","captionSegments":["图 16.11　(a) 路径经过各节点的概率；(b) 随机选取的一条路径。左图黑色斑点的面积表示相应概率，右图的黑色折线表示从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的样本路径。"],"id":"p257-b003","wide":true},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"kind":"paragraph","text":"我们用来数出通往 $B$ 的路径条数的消息传递算法，是和积算法（sum–product algorithm）的一个例子。“求和”发生在每个节点将前驱节点传来的消息相加时；前文没有提到“乘积”，但也可以把这里的求和看成加权求和，只是每一项的权重碰巧都是 $1$。","segments":["我们用来数出通往 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径条数的消息传递算法，是",{"em":true,"text":"和积算法"},"（sum–product algorithm）的一个例子。“求和”发生在每个节点将前驱节点传来的消息相加时；前文没有提到“乘积”，但也可以把这里的求和看成加权求和，只是每一项的权重碰巧都是 ",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"。"],"id":"p257-b004"},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"16.3　寻找最低成本路径","segments":["16.3　寻找最低成本路径"],"id":"p257-b005"},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"kind":"paragraph","text":"假设你想尽快从 Ambridge（$A$）到达 Bognor（$B$）。图 16.12 给出各种可选路线，并标明走过图中每条边所需的小时数。例如，路线 $A$–$I$–$L$–$N$–$B$ 需要 $8$ 小时。我们想找出成本最低的路径，但不想显式计算每条路径的成本。高效的办法是：对每个节点，求出从 $A$ 到达该节点的最低成本。可以从节点 $A$ 出发，通过消息传递算出这些值。这个消息传递算法称为最小和算法（min–sum algorithm），也称 Viterbi 算法。","segments":["假设你想尽快从 Ambridge（",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"},"）到达 Bognor（",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"},"）。图 16.12 给出各种可选路线，并标明走过图中每条边所需的小时数。例如，路线 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"I","text":"I","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"L","text":"L","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"N","text":"N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 需要 ",{"tex":"8","text":"8","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>"}," 小时。我们想找出成本最低的路径，但不想显式计算每条路径的成本。高效的办法是：对每个节点，求出从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到达该节点的最低成本。可以从节点 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 出发，通过消息传递算出这些值。这个消息传递算法称为",{"em":true,"text":"最小和算法"},"（min–sum algorithm），也称 ",{"em":true,"text":"Viterbi 算法"},"。"],"id":"p257-b006"},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-12.png","width":930,"height":510,"alt":"图 16.12：Ambridge 到 Bognor 的路线与边成本","caption":"图 16.12　从 Ambridge（$A$）到 Bognor（$B$）的路线图。箭头标明行进方向，边旁的数字表示走过该边的成本，单位为小时。","captionSegments":["图 16.12　从 Ambridge（",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"},"）到 Bognor（",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"},"）的路线图。箭头标明行进方向，边旁的数字表示走过该边的成本，单位为小时。"],"id":"p257-b007","wide":true},{"pdfPage":257,"page":5,"kind":"paragraph","text":"为简便起见，我们把从节点 $A$ 到节点 $x$ 的最低成本路径的成本，称为“$x$ 的成本”。每个节点一旦知道所有可能前驱节点的成本，就能把自己的成本广播给后继节点。下面手工执行一遍算法。$A$ 的成本为零。我们把这个消息传给 $H$ 和 $I$。消息沿图中的每条边传递时，都要加上这条边的成本。于是算出 $H$ 和 $I$ 的成本分别为 $4$ 和 $1$（图 16.13a）。同样，可算出 $J$ 和 $L$ 的成本分别为 $6$ 和 $2$；但 $K$ 呢？从边 $H$–$K$ 传来的消息表明，经 $H$ 从 $A$ 到 $K$ 的一条路径成本为 $5$；从边 $I$–$K$ 则得知另一条路径的成本为 $3$（图 16.13b）。最小和算法把 $K$ 的成本设为这两个值中的最小值（即“最小”），并只保留边 $I$–$K$、剪去通向 $K$ 的其他边，以记录进入 $K$ 的最低成本路线（图 16.13c）。图 16.13d 和 e 展示了算法剩余的两轮迭代，最终发现从 $A$ 到 $B$ 有一条成本为 $6$ 的路径。［如果到达某个节点的最低成本路径不止一条，最小和算法遇到并列时，可以随机选取其中任意一条。］","segments":["为简便起见，我们把从节点 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到节点 ",{"tex":"x","text":"x","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的最低成本路径的成本，称为“",{"tex":"x","text":"x","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的成本”。每个节点一旦知道所有可能前驱节点的成本，就能把自己的成本广播给后继节点。下面手工执行一遍算法。",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的成本为零。我们把这个消息传给 ",{"tex":"H","text":"H","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></math>"}," 和 ",{"tex":"I","text":"I","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></math>"},"。消息沿图中的每条边传递时，都要",{"em":true,"text":"加上"},"这条边的成本。于是算出 ",{"tex":"H","text":"H","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></math>"}," 和 ",{"tex":"I","text":"I","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的成本分别为 ",{"tex":"4","text":"4","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>"}," 和 ",{"tex":"1","text":"1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>"},"（图 16.13a）。同样，可算出 ",{"tex":"J","text":"J","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>J</mi></mrow></math>"}," 和 ",{"tex":"L","text":"L","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的成本分别为 ",{"tex":"6","text":"6","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>"}," 和 ",{"tex":"2","text":"2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>"},"；但 ",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"}," 呢？从边 ",{"tex":"H","text":"H","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"}," 传来的消息表明，经 ",{"tex":"H","text":"H","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow></math>"}," 从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的一条路径成本为 ",{"tex":"5","text":"5","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>"},"；从边 ",{"tex":"I","text":"I","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"}," 则得知另一条路径的成本为 ",{"tex":"3","text":"3","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>"},"（图 16.13b）。最小和算法把 ",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的成本设为这两个值中的最小值（即“最小”），并只保留边 ",{"tex":"I","text":"I","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"},"、剪去通向 ",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的其他边，以记录进入 ",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的最低成本路线（图 16.13c）。图 16.13d 和 e 展示了算法剩余的两轮迭代，最终发现从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 有一条成本为 ",{"tex":"6","text":"6","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>"}," 的路径。［如果到达某个节点的最低成本路径不止一条，最小和算法遇到并列时，可以随机选取其中任意一条。］"],"id":"p257-b008"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"从 $B$ 出发，沿保留下来的边回溯到 $A$，便能找回这条最低成本路径。由此得到最低成本路径为 $A$–$I$–$K$–$M$–$B$。","segments":["从 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 出发，沿保留下来的边回溯到 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"},"，便能找回这条最低成本路径。由此得到最低成本路径为 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"I","text":"I","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"K","text":"K","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"M","text":"M","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></math>"},"–",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"},"。"],"id":"p258-b001"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/figure-16-13.png","width":750,"height":1965,"alt":"图 16.13：逐步执行最小和消息传递算法","caption":"图 16.13　最小和消息传递算法：先求到达每个节点的成本，进而找出从 $A$ 到 $B$ 的最低成本路线。(a)–(e) 展示连续计算与剪枝的过程；节点旁的粗体数字是算出的最低成本，边旁的数字是走过该边的成本，最后得到 $B$ 的成本为 $6$。","captionSegments":["图 16.13　最小和消息传递算法：先求到达每个节点的成本，进而找出从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的最低成本路线。(a)–(e) 展示连续计算与剪枝的过程；节点旁的粗体数字是算出的最低成本，边旁的数字是走过该边的成本，最后得到 ",{"tex":"B","text":"B","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的成本为 ",{"tex":"6","text":"6","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>"},"。"],"id":"p258-b002","wide":true},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"heading","level":3,"text":"最小和算法的其他应用","segments":[{"em":true,"text":"最小和算法的其他应用"}],"id":"p258-b003"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"设想你负责通过一系列生产操作，把原材料加工成产品。你想找出流程中的关键路径（critical path），也就是拖慢生产的那组操作。如果把关键路径上的任一操作做得稍快一些，从原材料到成品所需的时间就会缩短。","segments":["设想你负责通过一系列生产操作，把原材料加工成产品。你想找出流程中的",{"em":true,"text":"关键路径"},"（critical path），也就是拖慢生产的那组操作。如果把关键路径上的任一操作做得稍快一些，从原材料到成品所需的时间就会缩短。"],"id":"p258-b004"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"一组操作的关键路径可以用最小和算法找出。","segments":["一组操作的关键路径可以用最小和算法找出。"],"id":"p258-b005"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"第 25 章会用最小和算法译码纠错码。","segments":["第 25 章会用最小和算法译码纠错码。"],"id":"p258-b006"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"16.4　总结与相关想法","segments":["16.4　总结与相关想法"],"id":"p258-b007"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"有些全局函数具有可分离性。例如，从 $A$ 到 $P$ 的路径条数，可以分解为从 $A$ 到 $M$（$P$ 左侧的点）的路径条数，加上从 $A$ 到 $N$（$P$ 上方的点）的路径条数。这类函数可通过消息传递高效计算。另一些函数则没有这种可分离性，例如：","segments":["有些全局函数具有可分离性。例如，从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的路径条数，可以分解为从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"M","text":"M","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></math>"},"（",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 左侧的点）的路径条数，加上从 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 到 ",{"tex":"N","text":"N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>"},"（",{"tex":"P","text":"P","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>"}," 上方的点）的路径条数。这类函数可通过消息传递高效计算。另一些函数则没有这种可分离性，例如："],"id":"p258-b008"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"text":"一队士兵中，生日相同的士兵有多少对；","segments":["一队士兵中，生日相同的士兵有多少对；"]},{"text":"一队士兵中，身高相同（四舍五入到最接近的厘米）的最大一组有多少人；","segments":["一队士兵中，身高相同（四舍五入到最接近的厘米）的最大一组有多少人；"]},{"text":"旅行商走访一队士兵中每个人所能走出的最短路线有多长。","segments":["旅行商走访一队士兵中每个人所能走出的最短路线有多长。"]}],"id":"p258-b009"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"机器学习的一项挑战，是为这类问题找出成本较低的解。寻找一大组取值近似相等的变量，可以通过神经网络方法解决（Hopfield and Brody, 2000；Hopfield and Brody, 2001）。第 42.9 节将讨论旅行商问题的神经网络方法。","segments":["机器学习的一项挑战，是为这类问题找出成本较低的解。寻找一大组取值近似相等的变量，可以通过神经网络方法解决（Hopfield and Brody, 2000；Hopfield and Brody, 2001）。第 42.9 节将讨论旅行商问题的神经网络方法。"],"id":"p258-b010"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"16.5　补充习题","segments":["16.5　补充习题"],"id":"p258-b011"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"exercise","label":"▷ 习题 16.3","text":"〔难度 2〕对于宽和高均为 $N$ 的三角形网格，描述图 16.11a 所示概率在渐近情况下的性质。","segments":["〔难度 2〕对于宽和高均为 ",{"tex":"N","text":"N","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>"}," 的三角形网格，描述图 16.11a 所示概率在渐近情况下的性质。"],"id":"p258-b012"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"exercise","label":"▷ 习题 16.4","text":"〔难度 2〕在图像处理中，由图像 $f(x,y)$ 得到的积分图像（integral image）$I(x,y)$ 定义如下，其中 $x$ 和 $y$ 是像素坐标：","segments":["〔难度 2〕在图像处理中，由图像 ",{"tex":"f(x,y)","text":"f(x,y)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"}," 得到的",{"em":true,"text":"积分图像"},"（integral image）",{"tex":"I(x,y)","text":"I(x,y)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"}," 定义如下，其中 ",{"tex":"x","text":"x","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>"}," 和 ",{"tex":"y","text":"y","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>"}," 是像素坐标："],"id":"p258-b013"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"formula","tex":"I(x,y)\\equiv\\sum_{u=0}^{x}\\sum_{v=0}^{y}f(u,v).","number":"(16.1)","text":"$$I(x,y)\\equiv\\sum_{u=0}^{x}\\sum_{v=0}^{y}f(u,v).\\tag{16.1}$$","id":"p258-b014","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≡</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></munderover><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>y</mi></munderover><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow></math>"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"证明可以通过消息传递高效地计算积分图像 $I(x,y)$。","segments":["证明可以通过消息传递高效地计算积分图像 ",{"tex":"I(x,y)","text":"I(x,y)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"},"。"],"id":"p258-b015"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"再证明，从积分图像可以得到图像的一些简单函数。例如，对于从 $(x_1,y_1)$ 延伸到 $(x_2,y_2)$ 的矩形区域，给出其中所有 $(x,y)$ 处图像强度 $f(x,y)$ 之和的表达式。","segments":["再证明，从积分图像可以得到图像的一些简单函数。例如，对于从 ",{"tex":"(x_1,y_1)","text":"(x_1,y_1)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"}," 延伸到 ",{"tex":"(x_2,y_2)","text":"(x_2,y_2)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"}," 的矩形区域，给出其中所有 ",{"tex":"(x,y)","text":"(x,y)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"}," 处图像强度 ",{"tex":"f(x,y)","text":"f(x,y)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"}," 之和的表达式。"],"id":"p258-b016"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"figure","src":"assets/chapter-16/exercise-16-4-region.png","width":550,"height":625,"alt":"习题 16.4：由 x1、x2、y1、y2 确定的矩形区域","id":"p258-b017"},{"pdfPage":258,"page":6,"kind":"paragraph","text":"积分图像示意图（习题 16.4）　$(0,0)$ 标出图像坐标原点；两条竖线分别对应 $x_1,x_2$，两条横线分别对应 $y_1,y_2$，用来界定待求和的矩形区域。","segments":["积分图像示意图（习题 16.4）　",{"tex":"(0,0)","text":"(0,0)","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>"}," 标出图像坐标原点；两条竖线分别对应 ",{"tex":"x_1,x_2","text":"x_1,x_2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>"},"，两条横线分别对应 ",{"tex":"y_1,y_2","text":"y_1,y_2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>"},"，用来界定待求和的矩形区域。"],"id":"p258-b018"},{"pdfPage":259,"page":7,"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"16.6　解答","segments":["16.6　解答"],"id":"p259-b001"},{"pdfPage":259,"page":7,"kind":"paragraph","text":"习题 16.1 的解答（原书印刷页 244）。　图 16.8 的网格上共有五条路径，因此如果均匀随机选取，每条路径的概率都应为 $1/5$。但逐个交叉点掷公平硬币的策略，产生的路径概率都是 $1/2$ 的某个幂。","segments":[{"strong":true,"text":"习题 16.1 的解答（原书印刷页 244）。"},"　图 16.8 的网格上共有五条路径，因此如果均匀随机选取，每条路径的概率都应为 ",{"tex":"1/5","text":"1/5","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>"},"。但逐个交叉点掷公平硬币的策略，产生的路径概率都是 ",{"tex":"1/2","text":"1/2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>"}," 的某个幂。"],"id":"p259-b002"},{"pdfPage":259,"page":7,"kind":"paragraph","text":"习题 16.2 的解答（原书印刷页 245）。　为了得到均匀随机的路径，在每个交叉点选择下一步时，都应使用一枚偏置各不相同的硬币；两个方向的选择概率应与各自传来的反向消息成正比。例如，离开 $A$ 后的第一个分岔处，从东边传来数“$3$”的消息，从南边传来数“$2$”的消息，所以应以 $3/5$ 的概率向东走、以 $2/5$ 的概率向南走。图 16.11b 中的路径就是这样生成的。","segments":[{"strong":true,"text":"习题 16.2 的解答（原书印刷页 245）。"},"　为了得到均匀随机的路径，在每个交叉点选择下一步时，都应使用一枚偏置各不相同的硬币；两个方向的选择概率应与各自传来的",{"em":true,"text":"反向"},"消息成正比。例如，离开 ",{"tex":"A","text":"A","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>"}," 后的第一个分岔处，从东边传来数“",{"tex":"3","text":"3","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>"},"”的消息，从南边传来数“",{"tex":"2","text":"2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>"},"”的消息，所以应以 ",{"tex":"3/5","text":"3/5","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>"}," 的概率向东走、以 ",{"tex":"2/5","text":"2/5","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>"}," 的概率向南走。图 16.11b 中的路径就是这样生成的。"],"id":"p259-b003"}]}